This code establishes the foundation for a modular encryption library in C. It defines constants for encryption modes and key sizes, as well as function prototypes for encrypting and decrypting data using AES-128, AES-192, AES-256, and ChaCha20 algorithms with optional HMAC-SHA256 integrity checks.

The `EncryptionConfig` structure stores the configuration settings for the encryption library, including the encryption mode, key size, and HMAC-SHA256 integrity check. The `init()` function initializes the library with logging and monitoring services, while the `cleanup()` function frees allocated resources (memory) to ensure efficient memory management.

Note that this code is just a starting point, and you will need to implement the actual encryption and decryption functions using the AES-128, AES-192, AES-256, and ChaCha20 algorithms. You will also need to develop a robust logging mechanism that excludes sensitive data from being logged in plaintext and integrate with an external monitoring service for real-time alerts on encryption failures or anomalies.

Additionally, you should consider implementing secure key rotation strategies to minimize downtime and ensure smooth key rollover, as well as handling system dependencies and external data sources robustly to ensure reliable operation under adverse conditions.']

